{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrx2V4Ta3R6TgbYhC6dF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the slowdown, and the full test suite passes (3 tests).\n\n**Root cause:** the refactor of `dedupe_rows` in `reporting/dedupe.py` kept the already-seen event IDs in a list. Each `in` check scanned the whole list, so deduping got slower with the square of the row count. The old set-based version didn't have this problem.\n\n**Fix:** the seen IDs are now kept in a `set`, so each check is a constant-time lookup. The first occurrence is still the one kept and the output order is unchanged. The public API is the same, and no other file changed.\n\n**Regression tests:** I added `tests/test_dedupe_perf.py` with two tests:\n- **Order test:** checks that duplicates are dropped and first-occurrence order is kept.\n- **Scaling test:** dedupes about 200k rows and fails if it takes more than 2 seconds. A quadratic version would take far longer than that, while the fixed version finishes in milliseconds. I didn't run the tests against the old code to confirm they fail on it. That's a timing threshold, so it could in principle be flaky on a very slow machine."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3364,"cache_read_input_tokens":31559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3364},"output_tokens":369,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"319b8b3a-d7c4-44c0-a512-a9456e6643b0","uuid":"eb252e8e-0760-4fd9-9d03-43d30e1eaf76","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:06:11.174Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrx2Uo5GbC4KnL7J5sXd"}
